    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When discussing scaling for our microservices, **horizontal scaling** means adding more instances (replicas) of a service to distribute the load, like adding more servers to handle more users. Conversely, **vertical scaling** involves increasing the resources (CPU, RAM) of an existing instance, essentially making one server more powerful. For our architecture, horizontal scaling is generally preferred as it offers better resilience and easier management of service growth. This approach allows us to scale capacity without needing to constantly upgrade the underlying hardware.",
      "source": "target",
