    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To proactively manage scaling, continuous monitoring is crucial to catch resource exhaustion before users are affected. We should specifically track **CPU Utilization** and **Memory Utilization** per service instance to determine when autoscaling triggers are necessary. Monitoring **Request Latency** is also vital, as rising latency is an early indicator that current capacity is insufficient, even before resource thresholds are completely breached. Finally, tracking **Error Rates (HTTP 5xx)** provides immediate feedback on whether our scaling decisions are successfully maintaining service health.",
      "source": "target",
